# 17. Switch Forwarding Behavior

This is a **high-value CCNA topic**.

A switch handles frames differently depending on whether it knows the destination MAC.

## Known Unicast

The destination MAC exists in the MAC address table.

```text
Known MAC
    ↓
Find port
    ↓
Forward only through that port
```

**No flooding.**

---

## Unknown Unicast

The destination MAC does not exist in the MAC address table.

```text
Unknown MAC
     ↓
Flood
```

The switch sends the frame out all interfaces except the interface on which it was received.

---

## Broadcast

Destination MAC:

```text
FFFF.FFFF.FFFF
```

The switch floods the frame out all interfaces except the receiving interface.

---

## Remember

| Frame type          | Switch action            |
| ------------------- | ------------------------ |
| **Known Unicast**   | Forward to specific port |
| **Unknown Unicast** | Flood                    |
| **Broadcast**       | Flood                    |

### Key rule

> **Broadcast and unknown unicast frames are flooded.**

