# 23. The Complete Picture

This is the key process to understand:

```text
PC1 wants to communicate with PC3
              |
              v
       PC1 knows PC3's IP
              |
              v
    PC1 doesn't know PC3's MAC
              |
              v
        ARP Request
         Broadcast
              |
              v
      Switch floods frame
              |
              v
        PC3 receives it
              |
              v
         ARP Reply
          Unicast
              |
              v
     PC1 learns PC3's MAC
              |
              v
    ICMP Echo Request
          Unicast
              |
              v
        PC3 receives it
              |
              v
     ICMP Echo Reply
          Unicast
              |
              v
        PC1 receives it
```

## 🧠 Core relationships

```text
ARP
IP → MAC

Switch MAC Address Table
MAC → Port

Ping
ICMP Echo Request → ICMP Echo Reply

ARP Request
Broadcast

ARP Reply
Unicast

Known Unicast
One specific port

Unknown Unicast
Flood

Broadcast
Flood
```

These relationships are the most important concepts from this lesson. 
